New suggestion...

That certainly stirred up some good discussion. I've read all the
responses, and on reflection is more open to abuse than legitimate
use.  OK, how about this then:

A "scroll of rescue".  It's like a amulet of LS, except if you die as
well as saving your life, you get rescued: ie teleported  - across
levels if necessary - to the spot where you read the scroll.  That way
you don't go "back in time" to retry things if you didn't like the
result; it's just the next turn.  The benefit is that you don't take
up a slot.  The drawback is that you have to go right back and do it
all again.

Maybe reading the scroll could produce the message "You feel like
someone is watching over you" (ready to rescue you - like a lifesaver
at a beach)



